    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, our primary offensive anchor with a score of 80.98. Facing Feltner (xERA 4.55), **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 13% boost in SP skill favorability and a prime leadoff spot that maximizes his ability to capitalize on our league\u2019s priority on stolen bases. While the remainder of the lineup falls into the \"marginal\" 50\u201360 range, **Colt Keith** (57.27) and **Carson Benge** (56.54) remain solid, if unexciting, plays. **Colt Keith** gains significant traction from Matthews\u2019 slow delivery, which our models flag as a high-probability environment for a stolen base, a key metric for the Zebras given the scarcity of the category.\n\nThe bench remains heavy with star power today, though purely due to scheduling\u2014**Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** are all sidelined by team off-days. Consequently, there were no difficult \"active\" bench decisions to make, though **Dillon Dingler** (44.13) was nearly bypassed in favor of a bench-deep utility replacement. The optimizer kept **Dillon Dingler** in the lineup largely because his xwOBA of .386 remains high despite the unfavorable dynamic platoon split against Matthews. We are keeping a close watch on **Lars Nootbaar** (53.90); while his xwOBA of .373 suggests positive regression, he faces a tighter challenge against Scott, and we have **Christian Yelich**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Hyeseong Kim** waiting in the wings should the situational data shift before first pitch.\n\nBeyond the core starters, the depth chart remains intact with **Rece Hinds**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Gary Sanchez** prepared for late-game substitution should we need to chase RBI or HR totals against tired bullpens. We are monitoring **Zac Veen**, **Nelson Velazquez**, and **Casey Schmitt** for potential pinch-hit opportunities. While we aren't facing an elite arm today\u2014Matthews at 3.94 is the toughest hurdle\u2014we must remain disciplined with our game caps. If **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, **Jose Fernandez**, or **Pedro Ramirez** are not showing elite efficiency in early innings, we will pivot to defensive replacements to preserve our remaining season allocation.",
